      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Heritage Park, opened in 2004, houses a 1919 Tudor‑style Wickers Building, a 1917 superintendent cottage, and a restored Interurban trolley car.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lynnwood%2C_Washington",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early 1900s Puget Mill Company sold five‑acre tracts to settlers, many abandoning high‑interest contracts, leading to Lynnwood’s first Interurban station.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
